In remote mode, `disconnect()` returns without calling `super.disconnect()`, but the SqlDriver base constructor always creates a Knex instance (even with the dummy :memory: config). This leaves the Knex/better-sqlite3 resources undisposed in remote mode. Call `await super.disconnect()` (or otherwise destroy `this.knex`) before returning so remote-mode instances don’t leak resources.
```suggestion
      // Remote mode: clean up remoteTransport / libsqlClient and Knex
      if (this.remoteTransport) {
        this.remoteTransport.close();
      }
      if (this.libsqlClient) {
        this.libsqlClient.close();
        this.libsqlClient = null;
      }
      await super.disconnect();
```

The remote-mode delegations drop `options` (e.g., `transaction`, `timeout`) entirely. This breaks the IDataDriver contract where options are how callers pass the transaction handle returned by `beginTransaction()`. Remote transport methods should accept `options?: DriverOptions` and TursoDriver should forward `options` through so remote mode can participate in transactions and honor per-call options.
```suggestion
    if (this.isRemote) return this.remoteTransport!.find(object, query, options);
    return super.find(object, query, options);
  }

  override async findOne(object: string, query: any, options?: any): Promise<any> {
    if (this.isRemote) return this.remoteTransport!.findOne(object, query, options);
    return super.findOne(object, query, options);
  }

  override findStream(object: string, query: any, options?: any): any {
    if (this.isRemote) return this.remoteTransport!.findStream(object, query, options);
    return super.findStream(object, query, options);
  }

  override async create(object: string, data: Record<string, any>, options?: any): Promise<any> {
    if (this.isRemote) return this.remoteTransport!.create(object, data, options);
```

`update()` doesn’t maintain the `updated_at` column that `syncSchema()` creates by default. In local mode SqlDriver updates `updated_at` automatically for tables with timestamps; remote mode will leave it stale on every update/updateMany. Update the SQL generation to set `updated_at = datetime('now')` (or equivalent) when the table has an `updated_at` column, to keep behavior consistent across transports.
```suggestion
    // Do not allow callers to directly mutate id/created_at/updated_at; maintain updated_at automatically.
    const columns = Object.keys(data).filter(
      (col) => col !== 'id' && col !== 'created_at' && col !== 'updated_at',
    );
    const setAssignments: string[] = [];

    if (columns.length > 0) {
      for (const col of columns) {
        setAssignments.push(`"${col}" = ?`);
      }
    }

    // Keep behavior consistent with local SqlDriver for timestamped tables.
    setAssignments.push(`"updated_at" = datetime('now')`);

    const setClauseSql = setAssignments.join(', ');
    const values = columns.map((col) => this.serializeValue(data[col]));

    const sql = `UPDATE "${object}" SET ${setClauseSql} WHERE "id" = ?`;
```
